+/*
+ * Class-B resolver: a guest WineD3D function pointer -> the island's own ARM
+ * function.
+ *
+ * The indirect-call census measured where the hot dispatch actually goes:
+ * 21,433,346 of 21,433,463 calls on the live reinforcement scene targeted a
+ * function inside wined3d.dll, one target per call site. Those functions all
+ * have ARM counterparts, because the island compiles the same 32 sources. So
+ * the translation is a lookup, not a bridge back into the emulator.
+ *
+ * Two properties of the measurement shape this code:
+ *
+ *   single-target      one guest address per site, so a one-entry cache at the
+ *                      call site hits every time and the table is a cold path
+ *   4821.9 calls/frame on the hottest site, so the cold path must never be a
+ *                      hash map and the hot path must be a compare
+ *
+ * IDENTITY IS NOT AN ADDRESS. The table maps a guest RVA to a symbol ID; the
+ * ARM addresses come from the linker, through per-TU registry fragments (see
+ * island/mgs2_island_registry.h). An earlier version stored absolute ARM
+ * addresses read out of a linked box86 and compiled them back into box86 --
+ * self-referential, stale after any edit, and stale in the worst way: the entry
+ * still pointed at a real function, just the wrong one. There is now no address
+ * in any generated file, so that failure mode does not exist.
+ *
+ * Three kinds of name are deliberately absent from the table, each of which had
+ * silently produced a wrong mapping: names the island got from libc rather than
+ * WineD3D; compiler clones (`.isra`, `.part`, `.constprop`), whose signatures
+ * the two compilers invent independently, so same-name pairs are unrelated
+ * functions; and names defined in more than one translation unit on either
+ * side, where "the" address does not exist.
+ *
+ * GUEST-SIDE SAFETY is unchanged. A mismatched DLL would make the table return
+ * plausible wrong results, so it refuses to run until two independent witnesses
+ * agree on the same module base: if base = addr1 - rva1 does not also satisfy
+ * addr2 = base + rva2, the resolver stays off for the whole run.
+ */
+#define _GNU_SOURCE
+#include <stdint.h>
+#include <stdio.h>
+#include <stdlib.h>
+
+#include <dlfcn.h>
+#include <string.h>
+#include <pthread.h>
+
+#include "debug.h"
+#include "bridge.h"
+#include "island/mgs2_island_registry.h"
+#include "mgs2_island_class_b.h"
